 and its container proved it - the reading is the\n18: # first command below. A db reset alone would have left that container in place, and every\n19: # check in step 5 would have measured the OLD setting.\n20: \n21: ===== BEFORE: the running auth container's confirmation setting - GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true means confirmations are OFF =====\n22: $ docker inspect supabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | Select-String -Pattern \"AUTOCONFIRM|RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL\"\n23: \n24: GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true\n25: GOTRUE_SMS_AUTOCONFIRM=true\n26: GOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000\n27: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n28: \n29: ===== bun run db:stop =====\n30: $ bun run db:stop\n31: bun : $ bunx supabase stop\n32: At line:1 char:1\n33: + bun run db:stop\n34: + ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n35:     + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase stop:String) [], RemoteException\n36:     + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n37:  \n38: {\"project_id_filter\":\"poancmeitlmxejofwzuu\",\"backup\":true,\"message\":\"Stopped supabase local development setup.\"}\n39: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n40: \n41: ===== bun run db:start - the stack comes back up, and its auth container is created from THIS branch's config.toml =====\n42: $ bun run db:start\n43: bun : $ bunx supabase start\n44: At line:1 char:1\n45: + bun run db:start\n46: + ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n47:     + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase start:String) [], RemoteException\n48:     + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n49:  \n50: {\"DB_URL\":\"postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres\",\"API_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321\",\"REST_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/rest/v1\",\"GRAPHQL_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/graphql/v1\",\"FUNCTIONS_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1\",\"MCP_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/mcp\",\"STUDIO_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54323\",\"PUBLISHABLE_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-publishable-key>\",\"SECRET_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-secret-key>\",\"JWT_SECRET\":\"<REDACTED-local-jwt-secret>\",\"ANON_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-demo-jwt>\",\"SERVICE_ROLE_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-demo-jwt>\",\"MAILPIT_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\",\"INBUCKET_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\",\"STORAGE_S3_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/storage/v1/s3\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_ID\":\"<REDACTED>\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET\":\"<REDACTED>\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_REGION\":\"local\",\"message\":\"\"}\n51: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n52: \n53: ===== AFTER: the NEW auth container's confirmation setting - GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=false means confirmations are ON =====\n54: $ docker inspect supabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | Select-String -Pattern \"AUTOCONFIRM|RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL\"\n55: \n56: GOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000\n57: GOTRUE_SMS_AUTOCONFIRM=true\n58: GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=false\n59: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n60: \n61: # MEASURED, AND NOT WHAT THE FILE SAYS: the auth container carries\n62: # GOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000 while supabase/config.toml carries [auth.rate_limit]\n63: # email_sent = 2. The CLI did not push the file's value into the container. So the checked-in\n64: # number is NOT the cap this run measures against. Step 5 check (f) reports the file's value and\n65: # whether the mailer actually refused anything; this line records why those two can disagree.\n66: \n67: ===== bun run db:reset =====\n68: $ bun run db:reset\n69: bun : $ bunx supabase db reset\n70: At line:1 char:1\n71: + bun run db:reset\n72: + ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n73:     + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase db reset:String) [], RemoteException\n74:     + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n75:  \n76: Resetting local database...\n77: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\n78: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_SECRET\n79: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_