ntinuous\n156: # integration has no database. The edge runtime CONTAINER that `supabase start` runs stays up and\n157: # still answers 401, which is the stack's normal state and not this launch.\n158: ----- the serve process was stopped by the executor after step 5 -----\n\n(End of file - total 158 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# AI4DEV-59 (email verification, unverified-write gate) - STEP 4: THE STACK WITH THE FLIPPED CONFIG\n# Started: 2026-08-09 18:27:51 +03:00\n# Worktree: C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\n# Branch:   nirdrang/ai4dev-59-email-verification-and-the-gate-on-unverified-writing-d2l1\n#\n# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT KEYS ARE REDACTED BELOW, exactly as the predecessor item's stack-up\n# transcript redacts them. They are local-stack values reachable only at 127.0.0.1 on the\n# machine that ran this, and nothing key-shaped is committed. GitHub push protection once\n# REFUSED a push in this project for exactly this file's predecessor, so the rule has a\n# mechanical enforcer. What is redacted: the publishable key, the secret key, the local JWT\n# signing secret, both demo JWTs (anon and service role) and the two S3 protocol credentials.\n# What is NOT redacted, because none of it is a credential: every URL and port, and the\n# postgres/postgres local database URL the Supabase CLI prints on every machine.\n#\n# WHY THE STACK IS STOPPED AND STARTED RATHER THAN ONLY RESET. Auth reads config.toml when its\n# container is created. The stack that was already running was created BEFORE this branch flipped\n# [auth.email] enable_confirmations to true, and its container proved it - the reading is the\n# first command below. A db reset alone would have left that container in place, and every\n# check in step 5 would have measured the OLD setting.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\\loop\\items\\AI4DEV-59\\stack-up.txt","text":"# AI4DEV-59 (email verification, unverified-write gate) - STEP 4: THE STACK WITH THE FLIPPED CONFIG\n# Started: 2026-08-09 18:27:51 +03:00\n# Worktree: C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\n# Branch:   nirdrang/ai4dev-59-email-verification-and-the-gate-on-unverified-writing-d2l1\n#\n# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT KEYS ARE REDACTED BELOW, exactly as the predecessor item's stack-up\n# transcript redacts them. They are local-stack values reachable only at 127.0.0.1 on the\n# machine that ran this, and nothing key-shaped is committed. GitHub push protection once\n# REFUSED a push in this project for exactly this file's predecessor, so the rule has a\n# mechanical enforcer. What is redacted: the publishable key, the secret key, the local JWT\n# signing secret, both demo JWTs (anon and service role) and the two S3 protocol credentials.\n# What is NOT redacted, because none of it is a credential: every URL and port, and the\n# postgres/postgres local database URL the Supabase CLI prints on every machine.\n#\n# WHY THE STACK IS STOPPED AND STARTED RATHER THAN ONLY RESET. Auth reads config.toml when its\n# container is created. The stack that was already running was created BEFORE this branch flipped\n# [auth.email] enable_confirmations to true, and its container proved it - the reading is the\n# first command below. A db reset alone would have left that container in place, and every\n# check in step 5 would have measured the OLD setting.\n\n===== BEFORE: the running auth container's confirmation setting - GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true means confirmations are OFF =====\n$ docker inspect supabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | Select-String -Pattern \"AUTOCONFIRM|RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL\"\n\nGOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true\nGOTRUE_SMS_AUTOCONFIRM=true\nGOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000\n----- exit code: 0 -----\n\n===== bun run db:stop =====\n$ bun run db:stop\nbun : $ bunx supabase stop\nAt line:1 char:1\n+ bun run db:stop\n+ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase stop:String) [], RemoteException\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n \n{\"project_id_filter\":\"poancmeitlmxejofwzuu\",\"backup\":true,\"message\":\"Stopped supabase local development setup.\"}\n----- exit code: 0 -----\n\n===== bun run db:start - the stack comes back up, and its auth container is created from THIS branch's config.toml =====\n$ bun run db:start\nbun : $ bunx supabase start\nAt line:1 char:1\n+ bun run db:start\n+ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase start:String) [], RemoteException\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n \n{\"DB_URL\":\"postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres\",\"API_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321\",\"REST_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/rest/v1\",\"GRAPHQL_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/graphql/v1\",\"FUNCTIONS_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1\",\"MCP_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/mcp\",\"STUDIO_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54323\",\"PUBLISHABLE_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-publishable-key>\",\"SECRET_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-secret-key>\",\"JWT_SECRET\":\"<REDACTED-local-jwt-secret>\",\"ANON_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-demo-jwt>\",\"SERVICE_ROLE_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-demo-jwt>\",\"MAILPIT_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\",\"INBUCKET_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\",\"STORAGE_S3_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/storage/v1/s3\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_ID\":\"<REDACTED>\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET\":\"<REDACTED>\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_REGION\":\"local\",\"message\":\"\"}\n----- exit code: 0 -----\n\n===== AFTER: the NEW auth container's confirmation setting - GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=false means confirmations are ON =====\n$ docker inspect supabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | Select-String -Pattern \"AUTOCONFIRM|RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL\"\n\nGOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000\nGOTRUE_SMS_AUTOCONFIRM=true\nGOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=false\n----- exit code: 0 -----\n\n# MEASURED, AND NOT WHAT THE FILE SAYS: the auth container carries\n# GOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000 while supabase/config.toml carries [auth.rate_limit]\n# email_sent = 2. The CLI did not push the file's value into the container. So the checked-in\n# number is NOT the cap this run measures against. Step 5 check (f) reports the file's value and\n# whether the mailer actually refused anything; this line records why those two can disagree.\n\n===== bun run db:reset =====\n$ bun run db:reset\nbun : $ bunx supabase db reset\nAt line:1 char:1\n+ bun run db:reset\n+ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase db reset:String) [], RemoteException\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n \nResetting local database...\nWARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\nWARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_SECRET\nWARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID\nWARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GITHUB_SECRET\nRecreating database...\nInitialising schema...\nSeeding globals from roles.sql...\nSkipping migration .gitkeep... (file name must match pattern \"<timestamp>_name.sql\")\nSkipping migration README.md... (file name must match pattern \"<timestamp>_name.sql\")\nApplying migration 20260808120000_accounts_org_membership_and_acknowledgments.sql...\nApplying migration 20260809090000_volunteer_github_link_and_imported_profile.sql...\nWARN: no files matched pattern: supabase/seed.sql\nSkipping migration .gitkeep... (file name must match pattern \"<timestamp>_name.sql\")\nSkipping migration README.md... (file name must match pattern \"<timestamp>_name.sql\")\nRestarting containers...\nA new version of Supabase CLI is available: v2.113.0 (currently installed v2.110.0)\nWe recommend updating regularly for new features and bug fix